WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.827
Treat each example as a small workflow rather than an isolated command.

00:00:04.827 --> 00:00:11.982
Before you run a cell, look at the starting table and predict what the shape or columns should look like afterward.

00:00:11.982 --> 00:00:15.598
Then run the code and compare the result with your expectation.

00:00:16.091 --> 00:00:20.783
Change one value, category, or condition and run it again.

00:00:20.783 --> 00:00:26.183
Pandas becomes much easier when you can visualize how each step changes the table.
